> **Fugus wrote: Sun Aug 10, 2025 5:35 pm**
> THEN you compare the 1% Dodge which is very good and gets better the more dodge you stack and the 1% run speed which makes you the fastest race in the game able to flee or chase down any other race more effectively to the Taurens 5% health which scales linearly.

Man, i'm playing with Night Elf Warrior right now and I can say with all certainty, **1% bonus to speed is so low that makes no diffence**, is't so low that you can't see a difference running side by side with other races, calling it the fastest race is an exaggeration to say the least.

If anything "Quickness" could be buffed from 1% to 2% easily, and as a fun fact, in early Vanilla the Dodge bonus was 2%, but for some weird reason Blizzard nerf it.

> **Larohir wrote: Mon Aug 11, 2025 9:38 pm**
> Racials are in a much better place than they were at launch—Classic racials were a mess.
>  .......

I agree with most of what you said, i will leave my suggestion of what changes could be made too:

 - Undead: Will of the Forsaken as passive ability, with (10% to 15%) of time reduction of fear, sleep and charm (the racial ability that **needs** a nerf);

 - Tauren: War Stomp shouldn’t reset the swing timer (like you suggest),War stomp also could be used by Druids while in any shapeshift form, without getting out the form, with this change Druids can have the same benefit from the racial like the other classes did, and lastly, give Gun specialization as a passive, so Taurens Hunters can have a small buff for the class;

 - Night Elf: "Quickness" bonus could be increased from 1% to 2%;

 - Dwarf: This one got a lot of nerfs with the recent changes, in this case "Find Treasure" should be removed, since addons like PFQuest have a "Chest tracker" making this racial completely useless, in the place could be put a passive buff to increase all damage, physical and magical by 1% helping the Dwarves offensively (already suggested here in the forum);

 - High Elf: The passive bonus from "Swiftness of the Ranger" could be increased from 2% to 3%, also a bonus of 2% Intellect could be included;

 - Goblin: This one have the worst racials by a good margin, here like suggested, the debuff/silence effect from the ability "Exit Strategy" could be removed, or at least change it to something less punitive, this effect could a reduction to attack speed and spell casting speed by 20% while you are under the effect of the ability.
And, they could get a new passive bonus, like, "Swift Brain" with a bonus of 3% Intellect and 2% agility;

 - Goblin and High Elf: Both races uses the starting stat points of the Orc (already mentioned in the forum), focused in strength and stamina, this should be change for better stats in agility and intellect, both races are intellegent and quick, with that, High Elf could use the starting stats from Blood Elfs from TBC, and Goblins could use Gnome stats as a base.

